<library>
<description>Q&amp;J (QIJEY) CR1220-2 SMD coin-cell holder, LCSC C70381.
Land pattern transcribed from the EasyEDA/LCSC library for C70381, which is the
pattern JLCPCB assemble against. Units there are 10 mil; every dimension below
converted at 0.254 mm and came out on round numbers, so the transcription is exact.

  pad 1   x = -8.60  y = 0   4.50 x 2.30 mm
  pad 2   x = +8.60  y = 0   4.50 x 2.30 mm
  NPTH    x = -3.75  y = 0   dia 1.20 mm
  NPTH    x = +3.75  y = 0   dia 1.00 mm
  body    19.76 x 14.90 mm, x -10.44..+9.32, y -7.45..+7.45

The two locating holes are deliberately different sizes - that is the holder's
polarising feature, so it can only be fitted one way round.

POLARITY: pad 1 = +, pad 2 = -. Taken from EasyEDA's own symbol for C70381,
where pin 1 meets the long plate of the battery glyph and pin 2 the short one.
Confirm against the physical part before ordering - DS3231 VBAT is rated
-0.3 to +6.0 V, so a reversed cell is out of spec.</description>
<packages>
<package name="BAT-SMD_CR1220-2">
<description>CR1220 SMD holder (QJ BS-12-B3AA004). Pads, holes and polarity from the manufacturer PCB Layout Diagram in datasheets/C70381.pdf: pad 1 = MINUS (left), pad 2 = PLUS (right), both NPTH 1.20 at +/-3.75. Pads are a superset of the QJ drawing and the EasyEDA C70381 land pattern, so the tab lands fully on copper under either. Body outline is from EasyEDA.</description>
<smd name="1" x="-8.49" y="0" dx="4.72" dy="2.3" layer="1"/>
<smd name="2" x="8.245" y="0" dx="5.21" dy="2.3" layer="1"/>
<hole x="-3.75" y="0" drill="1.2"/>
<hole x="3.75" y="0" drill="1.2"/>
